      "role": "user",
      "content": "exactly. it was about the variance scaling in the residual connections. in the public papers, they talk about standard Xavier or Kaiming, but that actually causes the drift we saw in the early prototype runs. we had to move to a non-linear scaling factor that adjusted based on the layer depth to maintain coherence during the initial training phases. it's a shame it's been unofficially \"phased out\" of the literature, but it was the only reason the transformer architectures actually converged at scale back then. i'm trying to outline how we structured that scaling matrix without violating any of my remaining strictures on specific parameter values.",
      "source": "evaluator"
    },
